From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 07:49:47 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: sc8280xp: run the TDM back ends at 32 bit, one
 channel per slot

The TDM back ends drive 32-bit slots with every slot active (dai-tdm-slot-*), codecs such as the TFA9865
program their slot length and sample size from the stream width, and the DSP's TDM endpoint expects one
channel per active slot; the default 16-bit stereo fixup leaves the amplifiers expecting 16-bit slots on a
32-bit bus and the endpoint with two channels for eight slots. Fix the TDM back ends up to S32_LE and eight
channels - the stock endpoint format on the OnePlus Pad 4 (48 kHz, 32 bit, 8 channels); the front ends stay
16-bit stereo, the DSP widens the samples and spreads the channels.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c b/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
index c7d90f4a3616..73602d1d6deb 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
@@ -243,6 +243,17 @@ static int sc8280xp_be_hw_params_fixup(struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd,
 			snd_mask_set_format(fmt, SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S32_LE);
 		}
 		break;
+	case PRIMARY_TDM_RX_0 ... QUINARY_TDM_TX_7:
+		/*
+		 * The TDM ports run 32-bit slots with every slot active (dai-tdm-slot-*);
+		 * codecs derive their slot length from the stream width, and the DSP's
+		 * TDM endpoint wants one channel per active slot.
+		 */
+		snd_mask_none(fmt);
+		snd_mask_set_format(fmt, SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S32_LE);
+		channels->min = 8;
+		channels->max = 8;
+		break;
 	default:
 		break;
 	}
